{
  "part": {
    "name": "Ergonomic mouse-style housing with scroll wheel",
    "description": "A streamlined, bilaterally near-symmetric housing comprising a closed freeform body, an integrated rectangular wheel-support pedestal, and a separate toroidal scroll-wheel solid. The main housing is bounded by six large B-spline surface patches, while the pedestal and wheel use planar and toroidal faces. The STEP model contains 2 solids, 2 shells, and 15 faces.",
    "source_views": [
      "front",
      "back",
      "left",
      "right",
      "top",
      "bottom",
      "toprightiso"
    ],
    "symmetry_note": "The main body is approximately bilaterally symmetric about the longitudinal vertical center plane, with closely corresponding left and right flank surfaces. Small differences in the B-spline bounds and the slightly inclined wheel/pedestal geometry prevent exact mirror symmetry. The front-to-rear profile is intentionally asymmetric, with a low tapered nose and a higher rounded rear."
  },
  "Section": [
