      "features included": [
        "large convex upper shell",
        "ergonomic palm-support crown",
        "rectangular wheel-pedestal opening/interface",
        "longitudinally sloped top profile"
      ],
      "function intent": "Provides the principal hand-contact surface, encloses the upper internal volume, and surrounds the scroll-wheel support interface.",
      "physical behavior": "The broad double-curved shell distributes hand pressure over the perimeter and transfers local loads from the wheel-support region into the side and end walls. Its crown curvature increases bending stiffness without requiring ribs.",
      "geometry": "One large trimmed B-spline patch spanning the body width and most of its length. It is convex in the transverse direction, rises toward the rounded rear, and slopes downward toward the narrow front. A second trimming wire defines the central pedestal interface.",
      "location": "Top of the main body, between the perimeter shell surfaces and above the internal cavity.",
